# Marks the repository root for oracle-core.
#
# Config files may write paths as ${ORACLE_ROOT}/... instead of hardcoding
# /Users/you/... or C:\Users\you\... . oracle-core finds this file by walking up
# from the config file, and from its own executable, so a profile keeps working
# after you copy it to ~/Library/Application Support or %APPDATA%.
#
# A marker file rather than a heuristic: looking for .git breaks in a tarball,
# and looking for a directory called "oracle-v37" breaks when it is renamed.
#
# Override with the ORACLE_ROOT environment variable. Do not delete this file.
